    "created_at": "2023-02-20T11:55:10Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-02-20T11:55:10Z",
    "body": "This comes from the following Wattsi code: https://github.com/whatwg/wattsi/blob/ec7934b1914df5cb60421890aa92e6b27f05594f/src/wattsi.pas#L1193C32-L1197\r\n\r\nI think this Wattsi code is buggy. It is trying to avoid you doing `<dfn data-dfn-type=\"attribute\" data-export=\"\">...</dfn>` or similar, since per https://speced.github.io/bikeshed/#dfn-export `export` would be redundant in that case. But what we have here is `<h2 data-dfn-type=\"dfn\" data-export=\"\">`, which should be allowed because it is not redundant for `dfn`-type definitions.\r\n\r\nI think previously Shepherd scraped our definitions regardless of them missing `data-export=\"\"`, but that was bad and the new Bikeshed spec infra rightfully does not do that. So that's probably what broke.\r\n\r\nI can try to fix this tomorrow. (The fun part is doing a local Wattsi build to ensure the fix works. FreePascal!!)",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
